    07/28/2021 For Nextera checkbook id 1300 I need to change how the patient responsibility is calculated if the is any coinsurance
        Typically if there is coinsurance the claims examiner changes the amount of the allowable to be what the coinsurance allowed and covered.
        In BCBS it is the medicare allowed amount.  Once the allowable amount is changed the amount the member pays is what webtpa processing determined 
        as the amount to be applied against the deductible.   @deductible + @coinsurance_amount + @copay_amount - @msa_total_used
        BCBS doesn't want us to change the allowable amount to what medicare allowed.  They want the deductible to be calculated on BCBS allowed 
        amount.  BCBS pricing is applied before medicare.  The claims examiners updated cob_savings amount and the deductible to be based on BCBS allowed amount.  
        The net_pay for medicare patient resposibility - net_pay (what webtpa paid) is what the member resposibility is. 
        Initially I was told  The only way to identify these records is if the cob amounts are populated, 
        the claim_procedure_benefit.coinsurance_amount <> 0.00. On 08/18/2021 they had me test  claims where sometimes medicare doesn't pay  
        due to MC Part B DED but we should still use the patient responsibility from claim_procedure_medicare.  So if there is 
        claim_procedure_medicare records we should apply the rules whether or not medicare actually paid anything. or if there is a cob deducted
        even if there isn't a medicare line.  In looking at a claim medicare paid more than we allowed, the cob_deducted was populated 
